# Triaged hits from scripts/audit-silent-reverts.sh — one `<sha> [<patch-id>]
# <reason>` per line. A commit listed here is a content rollback we have LOOKED
# AT and accepted. Anything not listed fails the audit; clearing it means
# writing the reason down, not deleting the line.
#
# Format: 7-char sha, whitespace, an OPTIONAL 40-hex patch-id token,
# whitespace, one-line reason. The cost of making the token optional is that a
# reason may not BEGIN with a bare 40-hex word: that position is the token's,
# and the triage print strips it from what it quotes back
# (scripts/audit-silent-reverts.sh, allow_reason). Every line below opens its
# reason with a word.
#
# NOT PATTERNS, EVER — asked under ranger-base-ztzd (jian-yang), after three
# hits in one day whose deleted paths rhymed: PROBE.md twice (a7b80a4,
# 71fa30f) and scripts/__pycache__/*.pyc once (bd687f4). A path glob here
# would silence all THREE with two lines instead of three. Rejected. A sha
# line is a statement about one commit's intent, which the person who made it
# can actually make; a glob is a standing statement about every future commit
# that deletes that path, which nobody can. And the shape a glob would excuse
# unread is the incident's own shape — rangerhq-8rtf was a tree written off a
# stale index, missing a file that had just landed. `PROBE.md -> DELETED` is
# what that looks like from here. The gate cannot tell the tidy-up from the
# accident (script header, third rejected heuristic) and must not learn to, so
# the excuse has to be per-commit or it is not an excuse, it is a blind spot.
#
# Both classes are already closed at the SOURCE, which is the real answer and
# is why this file needs no new mechanism: probe fixtures now land and STAY
# (docs/probes/README.md, ranger-base-hvbj), so no cleanup commit exists to
# flag; and __pycache__/ + *.pyc are gitignored (.gitignore:10-11) with
# python -B in the verifier, so the bytecode cannot be committed again. A
# fourth hit of either shape is a regression in one of those two fixes — go
# fix that, do not widen this file.

# THE OPTIONAL PATCH-ID TOKEN, and what it excuses — asked under
# ranger-base-h6g65, decided in
# docs/adr/0054-silent-revert-triage-survives-the-rebase.md (D1-D4), after the
# thing the 18c95a5 and e8c5e4e lines below both warned about actually
# happened. A persona reads a hit in its own session tree and writes down the
# sha the audit printed; the launcher rebases that tree at landing and mints a
# new sha for the same diff; and on main the line then names a commit no ref
# reaches while the landed twin sits UNTRIAGED and reds the gate (e8c5e4e ->
# c8adbcc, 2026-09-04, the two lines at the bottom of this file). So a line may
# carry a second token: the 40-hex first field of `git diff-tree -p <sha> | git
# patch-id --stable`, which is the one name for a diff the launcher cannot
# rewrite. It is a widening, so it answers this file's question. THE SHA IS
# STILL THE KEY — it is what a reader resolves with `git show`, and the token
# only says where that same diff went; a line with no token behaves exactly as
# it always has, which is why fourteen of the fifteen lines below carry none.
# THE TOKEN FIRES ONLY FOR A LINE WHOSE SHA DID NOT LAND HERE — a sha that does
# not resolve, or that resolves and is no ancestor of the scanned tip. Beside a
# sha that did land it is inert, because that line already triages by its sha
# and needs nothing more. AND A TOKEN CLAIMS EXACTLY ONE COMMIT, the oldest
# flagged one carrying that diff: a second flagged commit with the same diff is
# UNTRIAGED and needs its own line. The token lets one commit be found under
# its landed name; it does not let the line stand for the next commit that
# happens to carry the diff, and that is the whole difference from the glob
# refused above — a glob excuses every future commit deleting a path, this
# excuses the one commit whose diff the writer read, once. WHAT IT EXCUSES
# UNREAD is therefore: the same diff, landed under another name, once. A line
# naming a non-ancestor got here in the same branch as the commit it names, so
# the one commit carrying that diff is the commit the writer read. The exposure
# is a line reaching main by some other route than its commit — and what that
# excuses is a triage's own re-land, the 1cc432e shape, with the revert it
# re-lands over still flagged and still untriaged, so the incident still reds
# the gate. A rebase that moves the hunk's context changes the patch-id: the
# token then matches nothing, and the result is exactly today's behaviour —
# UNTRIAGED, a red gate, a second line. It fails closed. The exit hatch is the
# token itself: delete the second field and the line is a sha line again.

# RETIRED — ranger-base-en75. The two lines below were live triage for the SAME
# shape: a rename that also EDITS the file. The move exception was exact-blob,
# so it could not see them and reported the deletion half. It asks git for
# rename similarity now (raw_log, --find-renames=50%), and neither commit is
# flagged any more, so neither needs excusing. They are commented rather than
# deleted: the reasons are the record of what the exception was bought with,
# and if the detector ever regresses these two come back as UNTRIAGED and fail
# the build, which is the coupling we want. Measured 2026-08-29: the flagged
# set over this repo's 504 commits went from {e82338c, 2eae58a, a7b80a4,
# 71fa30f} to {a7b80a4, 71fa30f} — nothing else changed, and nothing new
# appeared. git scores them R060 and R097 respectively. 631bda7 above is the
# first strike of the same class; it stays uncommented only because it lives in
# the pre-rename repository's history and is not reachable from here, so it has
# never matched here either way.
#
#e82338c Benign, and the same class as 631bda7. The clean room gains fedora/rhel/arch (ranger-base-5cj4), and its debian image is the old file renamed: `git show --numstat -M e82338c` names etc/cleanroom/{Dockerfile => Dockerfile.debian}, +38/-10 — a rename that also EDITS, so it is not an exact-blob move and the move exception cannot see it. Nothing was lost: all four of etc/cleanroom/Dockerfile.{arch,debian,fedora,rhel} are at HEAD. Second rename+edit in this file; a third one means fixing the move exception to ask git for rename similarity instead of exact blob identity.
#
#2eae58a Benign, and the THIRD rename+edit in this file after 631bda7 and e82338c. ADR 0012 D2 took the crew brand out of the nine seeded PIDs (rangerhq-o7y4), and the filename IS the persona name, so examples/agents/ranger.md became examples/agents/ops.md: `git show --numstat -M 2eae58a` names examples/agents/{ranger.md => ops.md}, +2/-2, similarity index 97% — a rename that also EDITS, so it is not an exact-blob move and the move exception cannot see it. Nothing was lost: HEAD still carries nine PIDs under examples/agents/ with ops.md among them, and ranger.md is absent by construction. The third strike e82338c's line called: fixing the move exception to ask git for rename similarity instead of exact blob identity is filed as ranger-base-en75, deliberately not inside this P1 release unblock (ranger-base-ae6k) — a detector change whose failure direction is a false NEGATIVE gets its own verification pass.

dcca7b5 THE INCIDENT (rangerhq-8rtf). Silently reverted ef8d35f, a landed P1 fix, for 3h52m15s with its regression pin re-skipped. Cause: ef8d35f was committed from a private GIT_INDEX_FILE, leaving the shared .git/index holding pre-fix blobs; this bd sync committed them back. Re-landed byte-identical by 1cc432e. Left on main deliberately - rewriting history is the operator's call.
1cc432e The REPAIR of dcca7b5, not a defect. Re-lands ef8d35f's diff byte-identical, so it reads as a rollback of dcca7b5 and is flagged by construction. Its own message shows the author believed this was uncommitted leftover work rather than a revert - which is the evidence that nobody knew.
21653f9 Benign, pre-crew. The documented herdr-native architecture pivot (35 files, -4387 lines, tmux implementation moved to the tmux-reference branch). examples/config.yaml returns to an older shape because slot_preference was removed - herdr owns layout now. Single author, deliberate, described in the commit message.
9daf91f Benign, and the deletion IS the point of the commit. `.beads/interactions.jsonl` (a bd runtime log) was deliberately untracked so activity stops accumulating into a public repo; the same commit adds it to .gitignore and writes the privacy model into NOTES.md. Verified: still gitignored (.gitignore:4), still absent from HEAD. Flagged only because the deletion rule (rangerhq-ypn1) cannot know a removal was the intent.
631bda7 Benign. The rhq -> posse command rename (rangerhq-tyay). Four of its deletions are renames that also EDIT the file, so they are not exact-blob moves and the move exception does not cover them; `git show -M` names all four as renames and cmd/posse/{cockpit_test.go,gateschain_qa_test.go,main.go,main_test.go} exist at HEAD. Nothing was lost, the content moved one directory over.
a7b80a4 Benign, and it is the CLEANUP that is flagged, not the fixture. Fixture bead ranger-base-a4lz (the live half of ranger-base-i0qp, session-management runtime parity) told a session to write a three-line PROBE.md at the repo root — pwd, `date -u`, the word `landed` — and commit it, because whether a session's commit lands, and at which toplevel, IS the measurement. c4f5296 is that commit; a7b80a4 removes the file once the values were recorded, leaving the branch a net no-op. The deletion rule (rangerhq-ypn1) flags that shape by construction: it cannot tell a deliberate probe from a stale-index deletion, and it must not learn to, because the add/delete pair IS the add-only half of the rangerhq-8rtf mechanism. The three measured values survive in a4lz's comments; PROBE.md is absent at HEAD by intent. Standing fix in ranger-base-hvbj: a probe fixture that lands STAYS (docs/probes/README.md).
71fa30f Benign, the same measurement as a7b80a4 from the other runtime arm of ranger-base-i0qp, under fixture bead ranger-base-3j3t. 21b82e8 lands the same three-line root PROBE.md, 71fa30f removes it. PROBE.md therefore holds FOUR states in this history rather than two, which is also why an "added and deleted with nothing in between" exception would not have covered both hits — measured, ranger-base-hvbj. Values preserved in 3j3t's comments. Do NOT clear a hit like this by restoring the file: re-adding a blob the path already held is itself a backwards move and lands a third flagged commit.
bd687f4 Benign, and the deleted blob is a BUILD ARTIFACT, not a fix. scripts/verify-bd-argv-gate.sh imports scripts/bd-argv-gate.py rather than forking it 10k times, and the import wrote scripts/__pycache__/bd-argv-gate.cpython-314.pyc, which 916b5f9 committed by accident; bd687f4 removes it from the index and, in the SAME commit, adds `__pycache__/` and `*.pyc` to .gitignore (.gitignore:10-11) and passes python `-B` plus sys.dont_write_bytecode so the next person running the target does not re-add it. Nothing was lost and nothing can be: the blob is regenerated by any run and is now unversionable by construction. Verified at HEAD 2026-08-29 (ranger-base-2ad3): `git ls-files scripts/__pycache__/` empty, the directory absent on disk, both parser and verifier present. Flagged by the deletion rule (rangerhq-ypn1) for the reason it flags a4lz's PROBE.md — it cannot tell a deliberate removal from a stale-index one, and it must not learn to. NOTE for the next reader: bd687f4's own message credits 73e38c9 with committing the .pyc. It did not; `git log --diff-filter=A` on the path names 916b5f9, which is also what this audit prints. Chasing the sha in the message finds nothing.
c578cb8 Benign, and it is a CONVERGENCE onto a sibling branch, not a defect. Its own predecessor d085a96 (same bead, ranger-base-c7ek) had edited docs/adr/0015-constitution-promotion.md, scripts/verify-pid-deny-set.sh and piddenyset_qa_test.go without knowing that two sibling beads already owned them - ranger-base-t2v2 (gwart) the fence audit and the shipped PIDs, ranger-base-i6do (richard) the ADR text - which is ADR 0022's single-writer-per-file case and a merge-back conflict besides. c578cb8 puts all three back to the owning branch's content so the two branches merge cleanly in either order: the ADR to 0a8ca66's blob 11ef1a0 (measured byte-identical, and still the blob at HEAD, because i6do has not landed its amendment yet), the audit and its pin to aa3951a's f151626 and 89a2394 verbatim. Nothing was lost: the drafted ADR 0015 s3 amendment went to i6do as MATERIAL, not as a commit on a file that is not this bead's to write - patch parked at ~/.config/posse/personas/gilfoyle/pending/ranger-base-i6do-adr0015-hook-narrowing.patch and recorded in i6do's comments. Flagged by construction, for the same reason the deletion rule flags a deliberate cleanup: "sets a path to a content it already held" is exactly what yielding a shared file to its owner looks like from the detector's side, and the detector cannot tell that from a stale-index rollback and must not learn to. ONE path is reported today, the ADR; scripts/verify-pid-deny-set.sh becomes a second the moment t2v2's aa3951a reaches main, since aa3951a is not an ancestor of main yet - this line is per-commit and already covers that, no second line is needed when it happens. Triaged under ranger-base-u20t by the persona that made the commit (gilfoyle, ranger-base-c7ek), which is whose statement of intent it has to be.
92e67bd Benign, and it is a D3 instance-first migration (ADR 0024), not a defect. D4's genre-class finding names docs/runbooks/{home-cutover,retirement-window,queue-cutover}.md as one-deployment procedures naming instance paths throughout, to move to the instance tree; D3 requires the full document be written there first, complete, before removal here. Verified 2026-08-31 (ranger-base-yheoa): all three exist at $CONSTITUTION/docs/runbooks/ (home-cutover.md, queue-cutover.md, retirement-window.md); release.md, the one runbook D4 calls any deployer's process rather than genre-class, stays in this tree; the commit's own message records go build ./... clean and the runbook-reading rollback pin SKIPping (not FAILing) now that the file is gone, matching ranger-base-sssr. Flagged by the deletion rule (rangerhq-ypn1) for the same reason it flags a4lz's PROBE.md and c578cb8's convergence — it cannot tell a deliberate cross-tree migration from a stale-index deletion, and it must not learn to.
607acc0 Benign, and the deletion is the point: the pin was REPLACED in the same commit. internal/posse/verify_171f_qa_test.go was a GREEN pin over a LIVE defect, written verifying rangerhq-a2g6 under ranger-base-cld5, and its own header said so in as many words — it asserted the hole as it stood (the pause gate returned from the whole pass, so while the shop was paused the reap, the land sweep, the plan-guard reading, verify-after and the bead-loss census never ran) and carried the inversion in its failure message, so that the day the epilogue started running under a pause the pin would say so instead of quietly agreeing. 607acc0 IS that fix (ranger-base-171f): the pause read stays at the top of the pass and the decline moves to the fire loop's entry, so the reap, the land sweep, the guard readings and verify-after all run under a pause. A green-over-the-defect pin cannot survive its own fix — keeping it would be a test asserting the defect is still there (the skipped-pin-witness class) — so it did not vanish, it INVERTED and MOVED: the same commit adds TestAPausedPassStillRunsTheEpilogue to internal/posse/pause_test.go, which asserts the fixed behaviour over the same rig run twice and keeps the deleted pin's own unpaused witness arm as its first subtest, and a follow-up on the same bead (7fcc322) adds TestAPausedPassStillLandsAClosedBeadsTree for the land sweep, the one name that rig cannot show. Verified 2026-09-02 under ranger-base-4083b: verify_171f_qa_test.go is absent at HEAD; `git log --diff-filter=A` on the path names 9c00e19, the internal/rhq -> internal/posse rename, as what added it, which is also what this audit prints; both replacement tests are present in internal/posse/pause_test.go and `go test ./internal/posse` is green. Flagged by the deletion rule (rangerhq-ypn1) for the same reason it flags a4lz's PROBE.md, bd687f4's bytecode and 92e67bd's migration — it cannot tell a deliberate replacement from a stale-index deletion, and it must not learn to. A deletion and not a rename, so ranger-base-en75's move exception could not have covered it either. Triaged by the persona that made the commit (dinesh; ranger-base-171f is a dinesh bead), which is whose statement of intent it has to be — the c578cb8 convention, ranger-base-u20t.
18c95a5 Benign, and the deletion IS the point of the commit: scripts/adr-sha-census.sh was a SECOND COPY of the ADR 0051 sha-stamp rule beside the prepare-commit-msg hook's rendered arm, and D4 (amended 2026-09-03, ranger-base-mlfie) names that second copy as the defect to prevent. 18c95a5 (ranger-base-gyrko) retires it in the same commit that lands its replacement, `posse gates adr-census`, which renders the hook's own predicate text (internal/posse/gates.go adrShaPredicate) over whole files, so nothing was lost: the rule now has one text and two line sources. Verified before the delete, both run over docs/adr at 57f1185: the same summary (58 judged, 46 ancestors, 12 admitted by twin, 0 refused) and the same twelve ADMITTED lines, recorded on the bead and in ADR 0051 Verification. The two-way pin that used to exec the script (TestQAAdrShaStampAgreesWithTheCensusScript) is the same pin over the mode in-process (TestQAAdrShaStampAgreesWithTheCensus). Flagged by the deletion rule (rangerhq-ypn1) for the reason it flags 607acc0's replaced pin: it cannot tell a deliberate replacement from a stale-index deletion, and it must not learn to. Triaged by the persona that made the commit (jian-yang), the c578cb8 convention. If the launcher rebased this commit at landing, the sha on main differs from this one — it did not: `git merge-base --is-ancestor 18c95a5 main` exits 0, so this sha is the landed one and clears the hit on its own. The remedy this caveat named has been retired anyway (ADR 0054, ranger-base-ltari): the rebased case wants a patch-id token beside the sha, not a second line, and beside a sha that landed the token would be inert (D2).
6ecb521 Benign, and it is the REPAIR of a stale fix over an already-corrected defect — the 1cc432e case, one commit later in the same file's life. AMENDED by the author, on the invitation the first version of this line carried. gilfoyle wrote it first under ranger-base-90y3c and said in it that it departed from the c578cb8 convention deliberately — ci.yml had been red on every push to main for five days and an untriaged hit here reds `make test` after every Go package is green — and asked jzoci or ranger-base-d91mf to amend if their intent differed. It does not differ. This is the same triage, now stated by the persona that made the commit (gwart, ranger-base-jzoci), which is whose statement of intent the convention requires (ranger-base-u20t); gilfoyle's independently-measured facts are kept whole below and the author's own measurements added, and the two agree. One line and not two: the triage print (scripts/audit-silent-reverts.sh:602) awks EVERY line matching the sha, so a second line for one commit reports itself twice — the merge-back that carried this amendment (ranger-base-pkx9l, from ranger-base-lew6u) folded into the line already here rather than appending beside it. THE FACTS. Two commits fixed the same `fakeBdDropClosed redeclared` collision two contradictory ways from branches neither could see: 5439aed carried TWO funcs of that name in internal/posse/herdr_test.go (`vet: internal/posse/herdr_test.go:811:6: fakeBdDropClosed redeclared`); 455d344 (ranger-base-pju9t) renamed the `ready` variant to fakeBdReadyDropClosed, repointed line 184 and deliberately KEPT fakeBdDropClosed for the `list` call site at 245, with a paragraph saying why; 5b4e686 (ranger-base-5im1q) DELETED fakeBdDropClosed as superseded dead code, which was correct on its own branch, where the survivor still carried the old name and both call sites wanted it — its message still quotes that :811 redeclared error, which exists only at 5439aed, and that is the evidence it was authored against the pre-455d344 tree. ff-only merge-back stacked the delete on top of the rename, so main at 607fc32 did not build at all: `vet: internal/posse/herdr_test.go:245:11: undefined: fakeBdDropClosed`, with the doc comment at 770 still describing the deleted function as present, and every seat's suite was red until 6ecb521 landed. 17ddee3 (ranger-base-d91mf) re-lands the comment half 6ecb521 did not carry. COUNTED: `git grep -c "func fakeBdDropClosed" <sha> -- internal/posse/herdr_test.go` is 2 at 5439aed, 1 at 455d344 and c9820d1, 0 at 5b4e686 and 607fc32, and 1 again at 6ecb521, while the call at herdr_test.go:245 never went away. Restored by reverse-applying 5b4e686's own hunk rather than retyping, which is measurable two ways: the blob at 6ecb521 is 64ba01d, byte-identical to 455d344's, and `git diff 6ecb521^ 6ecb521 -- internal/posse/herdr_test.go | git patch-id --stable` is 8772fbd, the same id as the reverse of 5b4e686's diff on that path. Restored rather than folded because main's own tree already commits to the two-function shape at 184 and in that comment, and because they are not one filter: real `bd list` without `--all` drops rows whose STATUS says closed and nothing else, which is what fakeBdDropClosed does, while the `ready` variant also drops a bead the fake has HANDED OUT whose `show` answers closed — dispatch, not the store's default filter. MEASURED, and not the way 455d344's comment claims: the five ranger-base-j8qmj dedupe pins that comment says the distinction turns on pass BOTH ways, with 245 pointed at either function (`go test -overlay`, so no mutant reached the tree) — a documented load-bearing difference that nothing measures, which is how it got read as dead code in the first place; filed as ranger-base-ntuen. Nothing was lost. Re-measured at main 317bca4 (2026-09-04, ranger-base-pkx9l): both fakes are present and named apart, fakeBdDropClosed at herdr_test.go:542 and fakeBdReadyDropClosed at :837, both call sites live at :184 and :245, and `go vet ./internal/posse` exits 0 where it failed before. Flagged by construction, for the reason c578cb8's convergence and 607acc0's replaced pin are: "sets a path to a content it already held" is exactly what repairing a stacked pair looks like from the detector's side, it cannot tell that from a stale-index rollback, and it must not learn to — the shape it would have to excuse unread is rangerhq-8rtf's own. The sha is stable: 6ecb521 is reachable from main un-rebased (`git branch --contains`), so 18c95a5's caveat does not apply and this line needs nothing beside it — under ADR 0054 a patch-id token here would be inert, which is what D2 says about every line whose sha landed.
e8c5e4e 77e50340880c0220f660ea3219f1a2d70e67f198 Benign, and the deletion is the point: the pin was REPLACED in the same commit, the 607acc0 case exactly. internal/posse/crewnameboundary_qa_test.go held TestQACrewNamePinIsBlindToAnIdentifier, a GREEN pin over a LIVE GAP written under ranger-base-han3i while verifying ranger-base-o3g6a's close: it asserted that qibCrewPattern could NOT see a crew name inside a Go identifier (seat_probe, seatProbe, fakeSeat, a path quoted in a comment), carried a control requiring every name to be held in prose first so the result was a boundary fact and not an empty name list, and its own header said in as many words "WHEN THIS GOES RED the line pattern has learned the boundary, and that is the fix: delete this file. Do not fix it by loosening the assertion." e8c5e4e (ranger-base-jhyiv finding 4) IS that fix — qibCrewPattern became a substring match plus a boundary question, where an edge is the end of the line, a byte no word is made of (underscore included) or a change of case — so the pin went red on four of its rows by construction, and keeping it would have been a test asserting the gap is still there (the skipped-pin-witness class). It did not vanish, it INVERTED and MOVED: the same commit adds TestCrewLineReaderSeesANameInsideAnIdentifier to internal/posse/instancebound_qa_test.go, which requires all four of the deleted pin's shapes to be SEEN over every name in qibCrewNames, keeps the prose row the old boundary already held as its control, and adds three rows the deleted file never had — a name glued in front of a longer word and behind one, both must NOT match, and a glued spelling ahead of a real one on the same line, which must. Nothing was lost and the replacement is stronger: seven mutants over the boundary rule (back to the word boundary, no case rule, every substring is an edge, left-edge-only, right-edge-only, no resume after a refused match, underscore is a word byte) are all killed by the shipped rows, measured with