ing the blind/headroom rows, the local pool meters, budget_pass/budget_day, uncounted_cap_ with its ledger and writability rules, tier safety and rolling dispatch are all untouched and green. Six mutants via `go test -overlay` show the replacement pins can fail, each redding the arm that owns it. Flagged by the deletion rule (rangerhq-ypn1) for the reason it flags 607acc0's replaced pin and bb6eb28's registry QA file: the audit cannot tell a deliberate retirement from a stale-index rollback and must not learn to. Not a stale-index tree either, the shape the rule exists for (rangerhq-8rtf): a stale index drops paths the author never touched, and all four here are the exact paths the removed mechanism owned, in a commit whose subject and body say so. Verified at this commit: `env -u GIT_EXTERNAL_DIFF make test` is otherwise green - zero FAIL lines, every package ok, internal/posse 846.8s, root 383.4s, cmd/posse 267.0s - and this hit is the whole of the red. Triaged by the persona that made the commit (gwart, ranger-base-6xx37), which is whose statement of intent the convention requires (the c578cb8 convention, ranger-base-u20t). The patch-id token is carried per ADR 0054 D1 because this bead's commit reaches main through the launcher's fast-forward and a rebase there would strand a bare sha; if it lands un-rebased the sha match is tried first and the token is simply unclaimed (D2/D3). One line and not two - amend this one rather than appending beside it, because the triage print awks EVERY line matching the sha (the 6ecb521 note).
